# Design docs

- Short beats long. Lead with the decision, then the trade-off: what we give up and why.
- State assumptions explicitly; if something is unknown, assume and label it.
- Architecture changes update the Mermaid diagram in `docs/design.md` in the same MR. Keep it to one diagram, numbered flow edges, OWASP tags on components.
- New or reversed decisions get a new row in `docs/decisions.md`; never rewrite history.
- Policy YAML, manifests and `docs/team-standard.md` are the sources of truth; docs explain why and link to them instead of restating numbers. The section 3 table in `docs/design.md` must match the policy and manifests.
- Run `python3 scripts/validate.py` after editing docs; it checks links, the section 3 table, audit-field sync and em dashes.
- Tables only for short enumerable facts; reasoning goes in prose.
- No em dash characters; use commas, colons or parentheses.
